 per render

`useKanbanCardMenus` builds the dropdown and the context variant of the
same card in one render, and both call `buildKanbanCardMenuEntries` with
the same processing flags, edit handler and plugin context. Every plugin
contribution was therefore built twice -- each plugin action's `items()`
ran twice per card per render for identical children, on a call the API
tells plugins to keep cheap and memoize.

`buildCardPluginEntries` now builds the two plugin-derived entries
(group "primary" and the `Edit` entry, which carries group "edit" actions)
from exactly the inputs they depend on, and `BuildKanbanCardMenuEntriesArgs`
takes them as an optional `pluginEntries` field: the card hook builds them
once and passes the same result to both variants, other callers keep the
internal build. The field is documented as valid only for a call whose
inputs match the ones the entries were built from.
