From 4e31e06652d6b3e873b723ea20683a97e7c0a61c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:40:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/23] fix(plugins): keep an explicit null icon, and finish
 the child-filter docs

Round 8 of the plugin-side loop checked the artifact against the claims made
about it and found two mismatches:

- `readSubItem` dropped a child whose `icon` was `null` (the idiomatic "no
  icon" a JavaScript bundle sends) along with arrays and objects, so a
  third-party bundle could silently lose a child -- and a single-child
  action would collapse to the flat item. The guard is now `icon != null`,
  and the snapshot normalizes null to "no icon". The upstream commit this
  was mirrored from accepts null; that behavior is now matched, with a test
  covering `null`, absent, array and object icons (the last two reported
  once, skipped).
- `docs/public/plugins-authoring.md` still described `items()` as running
  "on every render for both menu variants" -- the pre-perf wording -- and
  never carried the child-filter sentence the mirrored message claimed for
  it. It now says the variants share one evaluation and spells out the
  filter (non-blank unique id, non-blank label, callable run, boolean
  disabled, a name/component/element/null icon, unusable children dropped,
  repeated ids reported). PLUGIN-API.md's two mentions of the filter accept
  `null` too.
