From bb672a752b0b59641fd413bd9709a4d944f0d551 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:58:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] fix(plugins): recognise component-object icons and
 escape child keys

Two defects the PR owner found by rebuilding against this patch, both real:

- a valid child icon was dropped. `isUsableIconShape` accepted only
  `undefined`, a string or `typeof icon === "function"`, but React wraps
  `forwardRef`, `memo` and `lazy` components in an object carrying a
  `$$typeof` tag -- and `@tabler/icons-react`, the set PLUGIN_ICONS maps
  names onto and the icons plugins copy, builds every icon that way. A new
  `isPluginIconComponent` guard in `lib/plugins/icons.ts` recognises those
  shapes for both the child filter and `lookupPluginIcon`, so the plugin's
  own component renders instead of the puzzle glyph, and the icon-shape
  test now covers a `forwardRef` child.
- the `::child` palette suffix added in commit 10 did not make ids unique:
  a child id can still concatenate with a different action's key (`quick` +
  `pick-x` versus `quick-pick` + `x`). The child's menu key now delimits
  and escapes its id (`${parentKey}#${encodeURIComponent(item.id)}`), which
  an id cannot forge because a raw `#` in it is percent-encoded, and the
  palette passes that key through again as the command id. Four child-key
  assertions moved to the new format, plus a test for the colliding pair.

Also folds in what the owner reported as already-fixed on their branch
(`icon: null` accepted, the test helper's `items` typing): both landed here
in commits 12 and 11, so applying this patch supersedes those two commits
rather than duplicating them.
