From fbce2e5d42ae5dac9b6dcdfc61574bcb65ed8a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] fix(plugins): make child keys unforgeable and keep the
 native Edit item

Round 4 filed two findings; both are fixed here.

- The `#`-delimited child key was still forgeable, because the action id
  went into the key unescaped: an action id of `quick#x` produced the same
  key as action `quick`'s child `x`. Every key part now escapes the
  delimiter (`escapeKeyPart`), so a flat key cannot contain a raw `#` and a
  child key's first `#` always separates the scope from a percent-encoded
  id -- two actions cannot produce one key however their ids are chosen.
  Action ids are read the way labels are (`readActionId`: a non-blank
  string, else the entry is omitted and reported), and a test covers
  exactly the colliding pair.
