From 46b97e6cb98c9b9d14d2a9f02d07247c239ee43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:15:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/23] fix(plugins): drop lazy icons, encode key parts, and
 resolve own keys only

Three findings from the PR owner's rounds, all on code this patch owns:

- `isPluginIconComponent` accepted `react.lazy`, but a lazy component cannot
  resolve synchronously: a menu whose icon was one left the dropdown content
  uncommitted (suspended with no boundary) instead of showing the fallback
  glyph. The guard allowlists `react.memo` and `react.forward_ref` -- the
  shapes an icon set builds -- and excludes elements and bogus tags
  (`{ $$typeof: 1 }` used to reach `createElement`).
- The action key joined `pluginId` and `actionId` with a dash, so plugin `p`
  + action `q-x` and plugin `p-q` + action `x` produced one key, one React
  key and one cmdk value. Both parts are now percent-encoded around a `%`
  separator (`encodeURIComponent` always escapes `%`), and the child id is
  still encoded after `#`, so a child key can never equal a flat action's
  key either. Every key expectation in the menu, command and edit test files
  follows the new separator.
- `lookupPluginIcon` indexed the curated map with any string, so
  `"__proto__"` returned `Object.prototype`, `"constructor"` returned
  `Object`, and `"toString"` returned a function -- all of which React then
  failed to render, where the comment promises the fallback glyph. It now
  resolves own keys only (`Object.hasOwn`).

Tests: a lazy icon and a bogus tag are excluded (and resolve to the fallback
glyph), the inherited-key names resolve to nothing, and the two-plugin key
collision is pinned alongside the existing action/child pair. The public
guide's section is rebuilt from base so its diff is additions only -- the
formatter had realigned unrelated tables in that file.
