From 690b02dc94a3f40cb88d7c8ecc9a4ced16fefb00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/23] fix(plugins): force the flat Edit item over a prebuilt
 bundle

Round 9 filed five findings; three were already fixed on this tree (the
`forwardRef` assertion has been narrowed since the tsc run that flagged it,
both key id parts are percent-encoded, and the mis-titled throwing-getter
test was renamed), and two are new:

- a prebuilt `pluginEntries` bundle outranked `forceFlatEdit: true`, so a
  caller passing both silently undid the "never present the submenu form"
  contract the field documents. The flag now wins; the test registers a
  group `edit` action so the prebuilt Edit entry really is a submenu and
  the assertion fails without the fix.
- PLUGIN-API.md listed "an array whose entries lack ..." among the results
  that fall back to the flat item, contradicting the next sentence (and the
  code): a partly broken array keeps its usable children. It now reads "an
  array with no usable entry left".

The `buildCardPluginEntries` tests moved to their own file, which also
brought `kanban-card-menu-items.test.tsx` and the builder back under the
repo's max-lines limits.
