Subject: [PATCH 17/23] fix(plugins): encode key parts without throwing on a
 lone surrogate

The PR owner's round 5 found that key building used `encodeURIComponent`,
which raises `URIError: URI malformed` on an unpaired surrogate -- and
truncated astral text is ordinary plugin data (`name.slice(0, n)` on an
emoji, `label[0]`). These keys are built during a card's render, and the
board has no error boundary, so one such id would replace the whole kanban
route with the fallback; a lone surrogate is a non-blank string, so the
`readActionId` guard does not catch it.

`encodeKeyPart` escapes every code unit outside `encodeURIComponent`'s
unreserved set, `%` included. It cannot throw, it is injective as a
function of the input's code units (so a lone surrogate stays distinct from
any other id, and an id that merely *looks* percent-encoded cannot collide
with the id it spells), and it keeps both raw delimiters out of an id.
Reproduced first: restoring `encodeURIComponent` makes the new test fail
with `URIError: URI malformed`.

Also treats `disabled: null` as absent, matching `icon: null`: both are the
idiomatic "not set" a JavaScript bundle sends, and only a real type
mismatch should drop the child.
