From 0f6a9ee9fb614a28ecaf5c7bef1752cf3fdfe90b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] test(plugins): pin the escaping's width independence

The PR owner asked me to check the one property their own encoder got wrong
last round: a per-code-unit hex escape with a two-digit minimum makes `%0`
and U+0250 both encode to `%250`. This encoder escapes only `%`, `:` and
`#`, so no escape width exists to get wrong -- but the check is worth
pinning, because the property is what makes the design safe:

- `%0` vs U+0250, and `%` vs `%25`: escaped, so the pairs stay distinct;
- U+00E9 + "a" vs U+0E9A: untouched, so they cannot collide either;
- plus the existing `#`-bearing, lone-surrogate, two-plugin and two-child
  pairs.

The key tests moved to `components/plugins/task-menu-keys.test.tsx` with a
shared `allKeys()` helper, which also brought the older file back under the
repo's max-lines limits.
